 [Interpreted] That the headline is a negative is not surprising, and that is a point in its favour. Ghana is approximately 670 km north to south, human mobility along the north–south corridor is substantial, P. falciparum undergoes obligate sexual recombination in the mosquito, and transmission across most of the country is high. All four favour genetic homogenisation. The finding is consistent with the continental picture, in which West African parasite populations form a single major subpopulation (Amambua-Ngwa et al., 2019), and with the observation that differentiation within West African countries is weak relative to the differentiation between endemicity strata that Mobegi et al. (2014) reported between The Gambia and Guinea.
 7.2 What the analysis cannot establish, and why
 [Observed] Zone effects cannot be separated from region effects. Three of four zones are each filled by exactly one administrative region (Table 2.2). For those three, "zone" and "region" are the same variable. Any difference attributed to ecology could equally be attributed to the region — its health system, its drug supply, its sampling protocol, its collection year. No statistical adjustment can separate variables that are collinear by construction.
-Denominator for the batch numbers in this section. The study-composition and within-zone batch tests quoted below are computed on the 4,905 Pf8-QC-passing isolates — every one of them carries Pf8's own QC-pass flag, they are the set on which study membership and F~ws~ are defined, and they sit before the F~ws~ and clonality cuts that yield the 1,900 entering the population analyses (Guinea savanna 1,334, deciduous forest 337, coastal savanna 204, transitional zone 25). This single label, *4,905 Pf8-QC-passing (pre-F~ws~), is used throughout the document; "pre-QC" and "QC-passing" are not used as alternatives for it, because they invite a reader to think two different denominators are in play. So "1083-PF-GH-CONWAY is 100 per cent of the transitional zone, 50 of 50" and "transitional zone, n = 25" are both correct and describe different sets. Study nesting within zone is a property of the Pf8 sampling frame and is not altered by the later cuts, but the counts here are not the analysis-set counts, and the zone-pair overlap was not recomputed on the 1,900 set. The same denominator applies to the polyclonality figures in §7.3 and to limitation 2 in §9.1. Note separately that the marker panel in §7.5 carries a third* set of denominators: it is computed on the 1,900 analysed isolates but reports a per-codon called count, 1,834–1,900 depending on the codon, because a mixed call leaves a codon uncalled rather than being resolved to a residue.
-[Observed] Zone effects cannot be separated from sequencing-study effects either. This confounder was absent from the previous draft and is at least as serious as the collinearity above. Pf8 isolates arrive through named partner studies, and in Ghana those studies are almost perfectly nested within zones: four of six zone pairs share no sequencing study at all, including Coastal savanna vs Guinea savanna, the pair that produces the maximum F~ST~ and the polyclonality contrast. Three of the four zones are dominated by a single study — the transitional zone is one study outright (50 of 50 isolates, 1083-PF-GH-CONWAY), coastal savanna 89 per cent one study (387 of 435), Guinea savanna 74 per cent one study (2,678 of 3,605) — and deciduous forest is the only zone with no majority study, its largest contributing 391 of 815 (48 per cent). Batch effects in these data are demonstrable rather than hypothetical: holding zone constant so that only study varies, call rate differs between the six Guinea savanna studies at p = 2.8 × 10⁻¹⁹⁷, and between four of deciduous forest's five contributing studies at p = 7.7 × 10⁻⁸⁸ (the fifth, 1114-PF-PDN-DBS-GH-GHANSAH, contributes 4 isolates and was too small to enter the test). The Coastal–Guinea contrast has no within-study replicate and cannot be separated from a batch contrast by any reanalysis of these data. This applies with full force to the marker clines in §7.5: the pfaat1 S258L contrast runs between the two zones that share no study. See §9.1, limitation 2.
