 7.4 Practical significance
-[Interpreted] What the neutral result licenses. Neutral common-variant differentiation between zones is negligible — maximum pairwise F~ST~ 0.00232, with one of six confidence intervals spanning zero (Guinea savanna vs transitional zone, [−0.00083, 0.00178]), and the maximum staying within 0.00204–0.00255 across six threshold scenarios (Table 8.3) — so a spatially sparse design is adequate for characterising neutral structure. Marker-frequency representativeness is a separate question, and the rebuilt resistance panel shows significant between-zone variation at six of the nine panel genes, including pfdhfr, pfdhps and pfaat1 (the others being pfcrt, pfmdr1 and pfmdr2). If the question is whether a handful of sites will give a representative picture of the neutral genomic background, these data answer yes; if the question is whether those sites will give a representative picture of resistance-marker frequencies, these data answer no.
