 PI_MAF is not a MAF filter. The original text described the POD as "100,000 MAF-matched simulated SNPs". That is not what pi.maf does. In baypass_utils.R it truncates the simulated ancestral frequency to [0.05, 0.95] and binomial sampling then freely produces observed minor-allele frequencies below 0.05, so the POD is not matched to the observed MAF >= 0.05 spectrum. 0.05 is also simulate.baypass's own default, so setting it changed nothing. The "MAF-matched" wording has been removed from Sections 5.6, 6.8 and 8.1 as well as from this table.
